1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:18,280
Welcome to Update 18 of AHEAD Pathway: your evidence map. This is the most powerful thing we have built for you so far. It turns every reading, every note and every draft into one living picture of your study, and it puts that picture in your hands.

2
00:00:19,679 --> 00:00:53,160
At the centre is your own research question. Around it are the parts of your study, drafted from your own proposal. Every reading from your body of evidence is placed where it belongs, and coloured by what it does: supporting your argument, challenging it, extending it, or showing a method you can use. The dotted lines join readings from different weeks that speak to each other. And a dashed box shows a gap: a part of your study that still needs evidence. Nothing is hidden from you.

3
00:00:54,560 --> 00:01:23,560
This is where the power moves to you. Choose any reading and decide for yourself: which part of your study it belongs to, and whether it supports, challenges or extends your argument. Write your own note on it. Rename the parts, add a part, and place readings of your own, from your own searching, right beside the ones we chose. The map is drafted for you. It is decided by you.

4
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:46,260
Slide back through the weeks and watch your map grow. Week one, a few readings. Week five, a body of evidence with threads running through it. You can see yourself, the reading, the thinking, and the development. That is the story of your degree, and it is yours to tell.

5
00:01:47,660 --> 00:02:12,330
Every month, and whenever you ask, the map reads your evidence alongside your latest proposal or chapter. For every part of your study it tells you what the evidence says now, where it disagrees, what is still missing, and what it means for your own writing. And it gives you one clear next step. When you upload a new draft, the map reads it and moves with you.

6
00:02:13,730 --> 00:02:48,800
And all of it becomes one Word document: My evidence and thinking. Where your study stands. Each part, with its readings, your notes and what it means for your writing. How your thinking has developed, month by month. Your notes, as they came. Your own work over time. Download it whenever you like, and it is always the latest version. Bring it to supervision. Write from it. It is your working document, and it grows as you do.

7
00:02:50,200 --> 00:03:17,870
Professor Ojo sees your map, what it says and your notes, so that together we can see your thinking develop. But the map is yours. Open the Body of evidence, choose Open your evidence map, and make it your own. Your evidence, your thinking, your study. The power is in your hands. That is AHEAD Pathway: your degree, well supported, every step of the way.
